# Historical evidence binding audit checklist

- [ ] Frozen manifests retain their exact original repo-relative path identities and hashes.
- [ ] Retired active-root identities map only to the canonical current migration targets.
- [ ] A matching regular current file is preferred; a symlink or non-file fails closed.
- [ ] Current byte drift never satisfies a frozen binding and only triggers pinned-Git verification.
- [ ] The fallback commit is a full immutable SHA from before current-repo reconstruction.
- [ ] Missing, unreadable, wrong-size or wrong-hash historical blobs fail closed.
- [ ] Historical tree listings are rooted, canonical, non-empty and cannot escape their requested prefixes.
- [ ] Git access is local and read-only; validation never checks out files or mutates history.
